&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Asia-Pacific Marketing team’s mission is to engage priority audiences through impactful and relevant marketing campaigns and events, driving awareness, growth, and adoption of Stripe’s solutions. The Executive Marketing role is closely aligned with sales, collaborating with the GTM organization, including Sales and Partnerships. This role spans all customer segment executives (especially focused on must-win, strategic enterprise and Digital Native Start-Up organisations. As a marketing leadership position for APAC, it offers a significant opportunity to build and impact the Executive relationships in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the APAC region, an Executive Marketing Leader for an enterprise like Stripe acts as a high-touch bridge between the company’s senior leadership and its most strategic users. The focus of this role is to position Stripe’s regional executives as thought leaders, increasing visibility and credibility in line with Stripe’s mission to grow the GDP of the internet. Ultimately, this role converts C-suite engagement into deep relationships and partnerships and measurable business outcomes, including brand consideration, strategic deal acceleration, and pipeline growth..&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive Engagement Strategy:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design regional frameworks for Executive Account-Based Marketing (ABM) that target high-value &quot;in-market&quot; accounts and active buying groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft tailored engagement plans for Senior enterprise executives, startups and ecosystem stakeholders to reinforce Stripe as the leader in Financial Infrastructure&amp;nbsp; and enterprise-ready organization to support all business models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing Executive Hospitality &amp;amp; Events:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee end-to-end execution of executive events, ranging from private executive dinners to the executive engagements (one to one meetings)&amp;nbsp; in large-scale conferences like Stripe Tour event platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure events are not just &quot;gatherings&quot; but strategic experiences designed to drive deeper account engagement and foster long-term client CxO level relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading Executive Programs for Corporate Events:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define event objectives, success metrics, and scope for major executive programs including Stripe Sessions and Tours and Customer Advisory boards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional workstreams (Sales, Product, Leadership) to produce executive engagement user-centric approaches that showcase newly updated solutions and market trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive Thought Leadership &amp;amp; Social Media:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Devise strategies to build an authentic, authoritative presence for senior Stripe leaders&amp;nbsp; (APAC CRO) on channels like LinkedIn,by partnering with Communications teams, focusing on value-driven education rather than self-promotion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize diverse formats—Partnering closely with Comms to increase APAC Stripe executive touch points via podcasts, articles, and short-form videos—to demonstrate industry insights and build organizational credibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Event Identification &amp;amp; Participation:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify high-trust, high-value &quot;niche&quot; executive communities and industry circles for senior leaders to join and increase Stripe’s connection to shaping the financial infrastructure landscape in the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive Engagement ROI &amp;amp; Pipeline Influence:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a data-driven view to measure the success of executive programs, using metrics like Net Promoter Score (NPS) and marketing-attributed pipeline growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate deal cycles by using first-party engagement data to refine executive programs and identify &quot;ready-for-conversation&quot; participants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building Partnerships &amp;amp; Relationships:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the key regional point of contact for senior management, senior leaders, and high-impact B2B users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Key Competencies for APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep Regional Expertise: Mastery of cultural nuances across hubs like Singapore, Tokyo, China and Australia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Mindset: Strong partnership with regional sales teams to align executive marketing programs directly with account aspirations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Influence: Ability to navigate complex global structures and influence stakeholders across Sales, Product, and Communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in interacting and engaging senior leadership inside customer and partner accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant B2B marketing experience leading an Executive marketing function across multiple customer segments, including specific experience in executive content, event management, partnership marketing, and high -touch executive programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in defining and executing Executive marketing strategies that achieve funnel metrics and KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills in English, with the ability to convey complex topics simply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership and collaboration skills across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience partnering with Sales teams on joint planning, execution with key account executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record as an Asia Pacific leader, collaborating with global marketing teams to drive strategic connections through executive programs and partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding and/or experience with CRM, account-based marketing, and event and sponsorship marketing tactics and technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI user proficiency&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A startup mentality with a bias to action and the ability to flex in a fast-paced industry and work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing fintech, cloud services, and/or software solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb organization and project management skills and the capacity to manage multiple complex projects at once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills and the ability to craft actionable insights from complex data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resourceful, creative and dedicated to achieving operational and creative excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering tailored marketing content and experiences for customer segments spanning from early stage startups to the largest enterprise companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the payments, financial technology, and/or ecommerce industries and partner ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success delivering executive marketing programs with and through consulting and technology partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an outsized opportunity to shape how the global economy operates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Finance Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Bangalore Finance Operations (BFin) centre is a hub for high-quality financial operations execution. The BFin team partners closely with Stripe&#39;s global functional finance leaders — including the global heads of Accounts Payable, Payroll, Monetization Operations, Accounts Receivable, and FinOps Strategic Enablement — to deliver reliable, scalable, and controlled finance operations. BFin is the execution engine: we process at volume, maintain quality, surface defects, and partner with global teams to continuously improve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the AP &amp;amp; T&amp;amp;E Manager in Bangalore, you will own day-to-day operational delivery across two core FinOps workstreams: Accounts Payable and Travel &amp;amp; Expense. You will directly manage a team of AP and T&amp;amp;E specialists, ensuring consistent SLA performance, high processing quality, and strong controls compliance across both functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on people management role. You&#39;ll set daily priorities, manage team capacity, and resolve escalations — while maintaining close partnership with Stripe&#39;s global AP functional team. You own local execution quality and serve as the Bangalore execution interface for both workstreams. When you identify process defects or systemic issues, you escalate clearly and partner with global functional leads on the fix — but the day-to-day delivery belongs to you and your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and Develop a High-Performing Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage a team of AP and T&amp;amp;E specialists; set clear expectations, run structured 1:1s, and build individual development plans aligned to BFin performance standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire for open roles within your function; assess candidates rigorously against the operational and behavioural standards required for high-volume finance operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a culture of accountability, accuracy, and continuous learning within the team — model the attention to detail you expect from others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage team capacity and coverage across AP and T&amp;amp;E workstreams, anticipating volume fluctuations and planning headcount and scheduling accordingly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own AP Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee end-to-end accounts payable processing: invoice receipt, PO matching, approval routing, payment run execution, and multi-currency, multi-entity reconciliation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain payment accuracy and timeliness; manage exception handling queues and ensure aged items are resolved promptly within agreed SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own vendor communication for payment status, dispute resolution, and statement reconciliation; maintain professional and accurate vendor relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure AP processing consistently meets quality thresholds and SLA commitments defined in partnership with the global AP functional lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own T&amp;amp;E Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end T&amp;amp;E operations: expense report review and processing, corporate card administration, out-of-policy item handling, and reimbursement cycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce Stripe&#39;s T&amp;amp;E policy consistently in day-to-day processing decisions; handle employee escalations with good judgement and clear policy grounding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Payroll where T&amp;amp;E reimbursement intersects with payroll processing cycles; ensure your team&#39;s outputs are clean and timely to avoid downstream rework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor T&amp;amp;E processing metrics and flag recurring policy violations, system errors, or volume anomalies to the global AP functional team for investigation and remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Quality and SLA Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and report on team performance metrics: processing cycle time, error rate, SLA adherence, exception volume, and aging buckets across both AP and T&amp;amp;E&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct root cause analysis on recurring processing errors; distinguish one-off mistakes from systemic defects, and escalate patterns to the global AP functional lead for process or system remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in continuous improvement initiatives led by the FinOps Strategic Enablement team; contribute operational insight to automation and AI-assisted processing projects that affect your workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clear picture of team quality week-over-week and communicate status proactively to the Head of BFin before issues become surprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Global Functional Teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary Bangalore execution point of contact for Stripe&#39;s global AP functional organisation; communicate volume, performance data, defect patterns, and capacity needs regularly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate process direction and policy updates from global functional leads into clear, documented operating procedures for your team; ensure adoption is real, not just acknowledged&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate process defects and system issues promptly and with precision — you own identifying the problem and its operational impact; the global functional team owns the remediation design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the Bangalore AP and T&amp;amp;E workstreams in global FinOps operating cadences and cross-functional planning discussions as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Steward Controls and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all AP and T&amp;amp;E processes operate within Stripe&#39;s SOX control framework; maintain procedure documentation at the level of detail required for internal and external audit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform and sign off on periodic control attestations within your scope; support Internal Audit and the global AP team during audit fieldwork as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify control gaps in day-to-day operations and escalate to the global AP functional lead and Head of BFin for remediation planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12–14 years of experience in accounts payable, T&amp;amp;E, or broader finance operations in a high-volume environment; you understand the full AP lifecycle from receipt to payment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of direct people management; you know how to set expectations clearly, develop individuals, and hold a team accountable without micromanaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep end-to-end AP process knowledge: invoice lifecycle, PO matching, exception handling, payment run execution, and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with enterprise ERP platforms (SAP, Oracle, NetSuite, or Workday) and T&amp;amp;E tools (Concur, Expensify, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience operating in a SOX-controlled finance environment; solid understanding of AP controls and what &quot;audit-ready&quot; looks like in practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with AI tools in a finance operations context — using AI-assisted processing, automation tooling, or AI productivity tools as part of day-to-day operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics-driven: a track record of building and owning operational dashboards; you use data to surface problems and communicate team performance, not just report status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a high-growth technology company or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to automation or AI implementation projects within Finance Operations (beyond personal usage — you helped design, test, or roll out the improvement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and proactive communicator: able to work effectively across time zones with global functional teams; you surface problems early, write clearly, and do not need to be chased for status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes This Role Exciting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll manage two of the most operationally dense workstreams in BFin — AP and T&amp;amp;E together touch nearly every corner of Stripe&#39;s vendor and employee spend, and your team&#39;s accuracy and consistency directly supports Stripe&#39;s financial integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll be embedded in a global FinOps organisation that is actively investing in process quality, automation, and AI-assisted operations — there is real, near-term scope to improve how work gets done in your workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll have close proximity to Stripe&#39;s global AP functional leadership and a direct line to the Head of BFin — your defect escalations get heard and acted on, and you&#39;ll see the improvements land&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll build a team and establish the operating standards for AP and T&amp;amp;E execution within BFin — this is a chance to define what great looks like, not inherit it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stripe is at a scale and growth stage where operational excellence in AP and T&amp;amp;E has real consequence — audit readiness, payment accuracy, and expense compliance all depend on you getting this right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is investing in building out its Creative Design team within the Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) to reach users across the globe. The team designs comprehensive ad campaigns tailored for various platforms, ensuring that every visual element aligns with our marketing goals and engages our audience effectively. We create net-new creative content and localize and adapt our work to meet the unique cultural and linguistic needs of different regions, presenting our message effectively in global languages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to advertising and web content, we produce high-quality designs for presentations and collateral aimed at large users and executive audiences. Our designs enhance the clarity and impact of our messages, making complex information accessible and engaging—whether for a client pitch or an executive strategy session.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designers at Stripe&#39;s SDC bring a passion for captivating storytelling and great design. They use design systems to tell compelling stories to a variety of audiences, and are well-versed at expanding, evolving, defining, and documenting flexible design systems that achieve bar-raising quality and consistency for the brand at scale. They are user-focused, business-savvy, empathetic, and inspiring. The ideal candidate excels across a variety of styles, crisply articulates design decisions, iterates quickly, and collaborates seamlessly with marketers, product managers, leaders, other designers, and cross-functional partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideate, design, and produce world-class design solutions—both static and motion—across a range of deliverables including presentations, posters, brand art, and signage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Steward designers through large-scale projects, providing art direction and ongoing guidance on creative strategy, execution, and localization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across a wide variety of mediums (physical, digital, and everything in between) to create immersive storytelling and creative content that brings Stripe&#39;s brand and product stories to life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring design concepts to life through storyboarding, comps, and creative presentations, iterating based on stakeholder feedback and internal testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with copywriters, static and motion designers, marketers, and ad operations to develop visionary concepts that engage a global audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor designers in best practices and ideation, fostering an environment where everyone learns and grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present ideas in a clear, focused way that builds consensus within the team and with stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and implement process improvements through automation and AI integration to enhance design quality and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–10 years of relevant design and art direction experience, with a focus on technical or product-driven companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of independently delivering high-quality work and influencing the output of other designers and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma, Canva, and the Adobe Creative Cloud suite (motion and statics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or mentoring a team of designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to express and communicate a brand through distinct graphics, patterns, motion, interaction, and experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on maker with the skills to effectively communicate concepts, direction, and decisions to teams and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance speed and quality, consistently delivering challenging, interesting, and pixel-perfect work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persuasive and receptive to feedback; able to clearly explain work, process, and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working flexible hours, including late evenings (IST), to collaborate in real time with global stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly detail-oriented, with a drive for pixel-perfect craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multidisciplinary creative comfortable working across different mediums and excited about experimenting with new technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior people management experience, with a track record of hiring, developing, and growing design talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced at facilitating stakeholder alignment and advocating for design quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

